# Security headers for static hosts that support them (Netlify, Cloudflare
# Pages). Ignored elsewhere – harmless either way. The API sets its own
# headers via helmet. A strict Content-Security-Policy is intentionally not
# set here because it depends on the production API origin; see README
# "Production Deployment" for a ready-to-adapt CSP example.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
